{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1490127-the-arrival-vacancy-and-entrenchment-overlooked-inheritances-homebrew","id":1490127,"title":"The Arrival, Vacancy and Entrenchment- overlooked Inheritances (Homebrew)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-08-14T06:30:03-07:00","id":1490127,"title":"The Arrival, Vacancy and Entrenchment- overlooked Inheritances (Homebrew)","content":"The Merger forces the spiritual half of the Beast, the Horror, to combine with its physical half, erasing the human part of the Beast.<br /> The Retreat forsakes the Begotten in favour of an unfettered Horror.<br /> The Erasure forsakes the Horror in favour of their human part, while the Inversion essentially seeks to eliminate all Horrors.<br /> The Divergence seperates the two to a certain degree into two seperate beings, whereas the Incarnate then talks about how a Beast can take control of their life and become something more by fusing their physical and spiritual halves.<br /> <br /> All of the above have one thing in common: they don't really talk about the <i>Lair</i>.<br /> The Lair is a Beast's home, their own personal corner of the Primordial Dream, a place where they are both at their most powerful and their most vulnerable, a places that passes as their soul. In the very first description of the Lair in the core, it was stressed how this primordial landscape is just as vital as the Horror.<br /> <br /> So, my brain thought that there must be some sort of Inheritance that focuses on this much neglected third half of the Begotten existence.<br /> <br /> How could this come to pass, and why would a Begotten chose this path over another? What follows are my bumbling thoughts on the matter.<br /> <br /> <u><b>The Arrival</b></u><br /> The Arrival appears to be a normal Begotten at first glance: they look the same, they still feel like kin and act like they did. They still Hunger, and Heroes are still a problem with their Anathema.<br /> However, the second they enter their home terrain, things change: Anathema do not apply while they are at the physical location of a chamber, nor can they be placed on them here. They can freely call upon their Lair Traits while there, and even inflict Nightmares in physical chambers as if present, albeit through focusing. At the physical locations of their chambers, Low Satiety Atavisms and High Satiety Nightmares always apply.<br /> In addition, even when they are not present, an Arrival may overlap the Primordial Dream Chamber with it's physical location.<br /> Finally, each instance of a scary, horrifying event inside their Chambers counts as a Family Dinner, as long as the Arrival observes them.<br /> <br /> Other advantages of an Arrival:<br /> The Arrival can perceive what happens in their Chambers and Heart by focusing on it. Nightmares can by cast this way, too.<br /> Arrivals have up to four times the amount of Chambers they usually would, as well as an additional three Lair Traits they gain immediately with this Inheritance. Most strikingly, they have no limit to the lair traits per scene, and gain +[Lair/2] rounded up on rolls to inflict them. This Bonus also applies to using the Skeleton Key and opening a Pathway to the Heart.<br /> Burrows are unlimited and maybe freely rearranged as an Instant Action.<br /> <br /> Chambers actively fight back against being collapsed by intruders, increasing the necessary amount of successes to 5 * Lair for a Chamber and 7 * Lair for the Heart. Each Roll takes three times the Beast's Lair Rating in minutes, and the Chambers rolls the Beast's Lair Rating as a dicepool to cause Bashing Damage every roll (defense or athletics may or may not apply, depending on the chamber and active lair traits).<br /> <br /> <br /> The process of Arriving:<br /> The soon-to-be Arrival cares deeply for their Heart and Lair, and spends a lot of time personally tending to it, and the Lair returns the favour. Rather than increasing their own power directly, they infuse a large part of power into the Lair. The methods for this might vary, but at least one case suceeded by Feeding to the point of reaching Slumber, and then sacrificing most of their health inside the Lair before forcing their Horror to do the same, bleeding out Satiety to &quot;water&quot; the Lair in their own sweat and blood repeatedly. Another way would be to attract Heroes, lure them into their Lair and kill one in each Chamber through heavy use of the environment. Or the Begotten lures Prey into the Lair to Feed, but spends WP to deny the Horror the food, instead letting the te<span style=\"font-family:arial\">rror of their victims seep into their Lair.<br /> If they do enough of this in short enough a time span, their Lair Blooms, and they may attempt to finally Arrive Home with an Extended Occult + Lair roll requiring 20 successes, each roll requiring 5 days. During this time, they explore the link between their Horror and themselves<br /> <b>Dramatic Failure</b>: </span>In addition to the effects of a failure, the character suffers \u20132 dice to his next roll.<br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Failure</b>: Neglecting the Horror and denying them their food causes it to take off in search for food. The Beast loses a Satiety to lure it back and satisfy its demands or has to abandon the Arrival, causing significant and potentially irreperable damage to his Lair.<br /> <b>Success</b>: Successes are accumulated towards unlocking the secrets in crafting his Anathema.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> The character either reduces total successes by his Occult, reduces the time per roll to 2 days, or gains the Inspired Condition<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>The Vacancy</b></span><br /> Where the Retreat and Merger focus on the Horror at the cost of the human, the Vacancy sacrifices everything in favour of the Heart. Maybe traveling to the Mother's Land left a deep impression, maybe they love being in the Primordial Dream, maybe they simply hated their Horror: Begotten reach out for this Inheritance usually due to feeling more connection to their Lair than to their Horror, maybe due to feeling they have more of a hand in shaping it. Similar to how people might have come to hate their spouse, but still feel nostalgic about the home they built together, a Begotten who is conflicted about their existance might find solace in their Heart, and even when they decide to end their life, want their home to be taken care of.<br /> Unlike the Arrival, the Vacancy leaves an almost empty house, which needs to lure in unsuspecting victims it attempts to torment or kill to earn enough fear to pay their 'primordial upkeep'.<br /> <br /> (Mechanics and stuff is to follow)<br /> <br /> The Void is probably one of the most unusual Inheritances, as the resulting genius loci/ haunted place is more a fixture of the landscape or a mystery than a character.<br /> <br /> <b>The Entrenchment </b><br /> If the Arrival is the Begotten taking their Lair as their rightful home and taking control over it as an expression of feeling only able to truly express oneself inside one's own home, and the Vacancy is leaving behind a thing once loved out of sentimentality, the Entrenchment is a desire to show everyone this one thing you have, even if it kills you.<br /> Essentially, the Begotten brings the Lair, and by extension the Primordial Dream, into the physical world.<br /> <br /> [will follow in seperate post]<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> All of the above is very much still a work in progress.<br /> <br /> Constructive criticism very welcome!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: What I am mostly unhappy with right now is the &quot;appears normal most of the time&quot; thing with Arrivals. I also feel like the extent to which they have to go for this Inheritance (essentially someone living through their house, making decorating and designing their living place their hobby/reason to live) needs to be reflected in a change at the core of their being, but wasn't entirely sure how to apply this. Losing Atavisms and Nightmares when outside their &quot;house&quot;? Would make increasing it harder though, which runs somewhat against the theme. Chaining their Horror to the Lair, essentially taking out one of the Ravenous drawbacks, at the price of increased periodical Satiety loss? Replacing Life/Legend?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","user":"Wormwood","date":". 08-14-2022, 02:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-14T14:13:00-07:00","id":1490183,"title":"","content":"I think your biggest problem is that this isn't really enough meat for three meals. The Lair itself is &quot;neglected&quot; only in the sense of its physicality. There's a reason why Lair is a Beast's power stat. Interacting with the spiritual aspects of a Lair is actually pretty important to a bunch of the Inheritances; just not directly. A Begotten can't understand their Horror without understanding their Lair.<br /> <br /> Arrival feels too much like just a bunch of awesome bonuses with no actual sacrifice or fundamental alteration to the Begotten's nature to call an Inheritance. What Beast wouldn't want to get all this, and what stops them from pursuing other ways of being? This simply lacks a level of finality to the story of an attempt to become a thing of legend (successfully so or not).<br /> <br /> Vacancy and Entrenchment are more resonant with the themes of the game, but really could just be one Inheritance with two examples of how to get there. In both cases the conclusion of the Begotten's story is to be subsumed into the legend of their Lair instead of themselves, and this results in a place rather than a ravening monster lurking in the shadows of the world and seeking prey in its own strange and unique ways. Inheritances should be broad enough to encompass multiple paths to get to them. If one deals with the power of the Beast resulting in the human side and Horror side becoming diminished in favor of the Lair taking on a legend of its own, there's no need to try to bend into knots making it into more than one Inheritance.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-14T21:39:30-07:00","id":1490215,"title":"","content":"Not enough suicide.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-23T06:32:06-07:00","id":1491087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1490127-the-arrival-vacancy-and-entrenchment-overlooked-inheritances-homebrew?p=1490215#post1490215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not enough suicide.</div> </div> </div> </div>Succinctly put what I feel is missing.<br /> <br /> I shall tinker about and return someday here. Considering making the Arrival a &quot;sacrifice the Horror to the Lair&quot; type of deal, essentially letting the Heart take the Horror's place.<br /> enfits: No more Ravenous Horror being out and about, maybe even reduced Satiety loss, staying full after a meal for longer, the aforementioned increase of Chambers and Lair traits, as well as greater ease in using Lair traits.<br /> Drawbacks: no noteworthy defense mechanism in the Primordial Dream, absolutely no Atavisms or Birthrights, no Horror-Form and thus no power boost when entering the Primordial, maybe even losing all access to Nightmares when not inside a Chamber or Chamber-like location (forcing the Begotten to feed more mundanely). Ending up with a character that is powerful only on their home turf and has lots of trouble when in different waters in addition to gaining a severy vulnerability.<br /> <br /> Vacancy is somewhat similar to the Retreat, so has suicide covered =P<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1490127-the-arrival-vacancy-and-entrenchment-overlooked-inheritances-homebrew?p=1490183#post1490183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think your biggest problem is that this isn't really enough meat for three meals. The Lair itself is &quot;neglected&quot; only in the sense of its physicality. There's a reason why Lair is a Beast's power stat. Interacting with the spiritual aspects of a Lair is actually pretty important to a bunch of the Inheritances; just not directly. A Begotten can't understand their Horror without understanding their Lair.<br /> <br /> Arrival feels too much like just a bunch of awesome bonuses with no actual sacrifice or fundamental alteration to the Begotten's nature to call an Inheritance. What Beast wouldn't want to get all this, and what stops them from pursuing other ways of being? This simply lacks a level of finality to the story of an attempt to become a thing of legend (successfully so or not).<br /> <br /> Vacancy and Entrenchment are more resonant with the themes of the game, but really could just be one Inheritance with two examples of how to get there. In both cases the conclusion of the Begotten's story is to be subsumed into the legend of their Lair instead of themselves, and this results in a place rather than a ravening monster lurking in the shadows of the world and seeking prey in its own strange and unique ways. Inheritances should be broad enough to encompass multiple paths to get to them. If one deals with the power of the Beast resulting in the human side and Horror side becoming diminished in favor of the Lair taking on a legend of its own, there's no need to try to bend into knots making it into more than one Inheritance.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with your assessment of Arrival. I think I was too much going for a Incarnate-feeling and should have left the original &quot;weakly and homesick when out and about&quot; in. See above ideas to remedy, do you consider those sufficient?<br /> <br /> I'd already considered Vacancy and Entrenchment to sides of the same coin, so I can see where you are coming from. Maybe you are right and two Inheritances are plenty to get out of this stray thought (not to mention that those are not really meant to be played in any meaningful capacity other than maybe an epilog).<br /> However, I still think the Lair, while, granted, is mentioned and plays a role in some Inheritances, never is truly the focus, which is why I started this thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","user":"Wormwood","date":". 08-23-2022, 09:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-23T07:04:06-07:00","id":1491090,"title":"","content":"Arrival (which probably also needs a different name really, the character hasn't gone somewhere new or anything) should exceedingly crippling to the Beast when they leave their Lair. To keep up with Arc's pithier comment, the Arrival seems like it should have a downside outside the Lair equal to if not greater than those bonuses in the Lair tantamount to being near suicidal for them to venture back to where their enemies can fight them without the protection of their boosted Lair.<br /> <br /> A relatively simple way you could make it momentous to even consider leaving their home: They take on both the Ravenous and Gorged Conditions as long as they're not home. They've invested so much of themselves into their Lair leaving robs them of all access to their powers, while also forcing them to feed, a lot, if they stay away for any amount of time.<br /> <br /> This also helps drive in the nail that this represents a final state of being. They have become their Lair, and if kept from it they will wither and die, while being apart from their dream-soul robs them of every ounce of supernatural might they had before.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-23T07:34:17-07:00","id":1491092,"title":"","content":"Well, being a little more constructive than glib, it probably pays to get more into that.<br /> <br /> The first set of directional mechanics for the suicides called Inheritances that should be paid attention to is that the two sets follow along the lines of Beast's two main anchors, Legend and Life, with the corebook seeing the Beast's human half in Life die to exalt their Legend, and visa versa with the Life Inheritances in the BPG. There's the obvious mentality behind that about the thematics and ideas behind Beast, but one thing that should be noted is that those are both rooted in something mechanical about Beasts as characters, <i>and</i> that the precedence for Inheritances involves understanding the elements of Beasts as things that have equals-and-opposites, where in with an Inheritance murderkills one aspect of being to exalt another.<br /> <br /> Now with that on the table, we should briefly mention that I don't think we could apply that to either Lair or Satiety, particularly with each other. Lair is the universal that empowers and motivates all of the others-arguably even the Life Inheritances from the BPG. Satiety is also pretty core to all of the Inheritances-you can see the short term hunger versus long term gains across the board.<br /> <br /> With the experiment here (and every other one that preceded this one, I guess &quot;genius loci&quot; is just too tempting a conception), I feel like the primary way to understand is to look at Lair through it's &quot;physical&quot; components, that the dichotomy is Horror vs Chambers, with the goal here being to construct Chamber Inheritances that subsume the Horror. It pays to think about what that means, to destroy the ego in favor of becoming a place of power(arguably, we'll come back around to that).<br /> <br /> One thing that immediately becomes of note is that you could reasonably make the argument that both the Legend and Life Inheritances we have are all Horror Inheritances, so on initial observation you could make the argument that there's room for Legend and Life Chamber Inheritances as well-except I think we can also agree that there's something incredibly at odds of a Life Inheritance also somehow abandoning the ego to be a place of power. Life Chamber Inheritances sounds and feels incredibly weird, is what I'm saying (though Kudos to anyone who figures that out). Still, in building these Chamber Inheritances, it can be helpful to think of them as Legend Chamber Inheritances, even if the Legend part is strongly implied to be silent.<br /> <br /> Finally, the directional mechanics of Legend Inheritances tends towards the extremes of the real, the ideal, and their synthesis(or the waking, the dreaming, and their synthesis, if you'd prefer)-that is, all that a Beast is collapses into either a physical form, an Astral form, or is brought together towards a pinnacle.* In similar fashion, it probably pays to conceive of Chamber Inheritances as all the Beast being poured into the physical, the Astral, or in synthesis.<br /> <br /> Two small notes include a) resist the urge to conceive of these Inheritances as anything that might be constructed with the Ephemeral Entities or the Horror Creation rules till the last minute-even if the idea is that there is still a sentience you can hang on those rule sets for these Inheritances, you're probably gonna land closer to intention if you construct it away from those at first, and b) it probably pays to think of how they warp and infect the people who deal with them rather than thinking of how they inflict and impose themselves on them (as uselessly vague as that is). Also, while they tend to be more powerful than what you'd probably want for this, looking at Chris Allen's Pangaeans is probably useful correlation, particularly the Really Highly Powerful ones, since those characters are more like setting pieces than individual antagonists.<br /> <br /> Final contribution, If I were going to try my hand at this idea, I'd probably land on something like &quot;The Haunting&quot;, where in a Beast collapses everything into a singular Chamber's physical location, &quot;The Nightmare&quot;, where in a Beast more tightly winds their Astral Chambers together and severs the Burrows to reality as much as possible, creating a shared nightmare people sleep their way into**, and &quot;The Labyrinth&quot;, which takes the way chambers work on both sides up to 11 sans their minotaur, whatever that means.<br /> <br /> EDIT: As a note on my own conceptions, I can see arguments for why a Beast would claim &quot;The Haunting&quot; and &quot;The Nightmare&quot;, but what I understand of my own &quot;Labyrinth&quot; concept? <a href=\"https://comicaurora.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/CH17_032_mercy.png\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;I didn't design them to do that. Who would, really?&quot;</a><br /> <br /> *Life Inheritances don't do this, of course, but they're openly intended to contrast the Legend Inheritances, so some of the rules are changed.<br /> **This is where &quot;place of power&quot; is arguable, because the Astral is a place-not-place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 08-23-2022, 12:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-23T13:05:30-07:00","id":1491116,"title":"","content":"As odd as <i>Life Chamber Inheritances</i> sound, could they be made to symbolise becoming a shut-in? The Begotten removes or suppresses the Horror, which ought to be the Id that drives them to interact with the world. Instead, they inhabit their Chambers full-time, whether in the Astral or in the material. They end up both isolated and protected in their little safe space.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-23T13:33:39-07:00","id":1491118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1490127-the-arrival-vacancy-and-entrenchment-overlooked-inheritances-homebrew?p=1491116#post1491116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As odd as <i>Life Chamber Inheritances</i> sound, could they be made to symbolise becoming a shut-in? The Begotten removes or suppresses the Horror, which ought to be the Id that drives them to interact with the world. Instead, they inhabit their Chambers full-time, whether in the Astral or in the material. They end up both isolated and protected in their little safe space.</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as I can wrap my mind around the concept, the general vibe that emerges from the Kingdom Hearts Word Salad that is Life Chamber Inheritances (a fragmentary passage) is more along the lines of killing yourself to further divide the real and the ideal, ala Wolf and Gauntlet courtesy Sundering. The two bits of named madness from the consideration that emerged were &quot;The Shadow&quot; and &quot;The Prism&quot; and I will make no pretentions to having spent time making sense of what my mind even meant by that for now. I'm sure after work would be a different subject.<br /> <br /> EDIT: as an idle set of thoughts on break, locations resistant to &quot;chambering&quot; and implied &quot;mires&quot; that muddy and realize the ideal rambled across my mind.<br /> <br /> Again though, everything in that word salad is kind of at odds with each other.<br /> <br /> As for shut in, &quot;the Nightmare&quot; feels more akin to that. It's not infeasible, though, that an word salad-garbage-float-by-days Inheritance could do the full &quot;chick goes back into egg, princes rule in coffins&quot; psuedo-True Fae shenaniganery could emerge from that, body and all.<br /> <br /> EDIT: A general moral to the thread-&quot;Don't go splitting Fisher Kings, listen to the nightmares and dreams that you're used to.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 08-23-2022, 05:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-24T04:21:44-07:00","id":1491180,"title":"","content":"There may be something worthwhile looking at \u2018demon lord does dungeon managing\u2019 \u00e0 la Dungeon Keeper and its derivative video games/ light novels\u2026<br /> <br /> ATM, I cast my votes for<br /> A) a haunted ground in the waking world, \u00e0 la Haunted and/or Sentient places from Hunter 2e, where <i>there is no actor</i> walking around; only an ambient silence reminiscent of the calm of the Primordial Dream as experienced by Beasts,<br /> <br /> and B) a fortified ruin-sanctuary floating all over the Astral (including the Bright Dream, but never the waking world), inhabited by a paranoid \u2018human\u2019 determined to strike down all invaders and interlopers even as he swoops down every now and then for \u2018supplies\u2019.<br /> <br /> EDIT: whereas A above would be the typical uncanny haunted locale you\u2019d see in urban legends/ghost stories/any cautionary folk-tales, B would be in contrast uncannily \u2018normal\u2019 and \u2018mundane\u2019 despite swimming in the Astral, almost as if you got back out to the waking world\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":". 08-24-2022, 07:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-28T01:22:16-07:00","id":1491566,"title":"","content":"Thanks, everyone!<br /> <br /> The more I read here, the more I feel like this fun little thought experiment will end up as a 4 dot merit somewhat based on Horror Spawn, but instead investing in a single chamber, simply termed Genius Loci, which allows remote-use of Lair traits, or bonus dice on connecting to that Chamber through Skeleton Key, or awareness of the Chamber similar to Horror Spawn etc.<br /> <br /> Anywho, back to topic:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1490127-the-arrival-vacancy-and-entrenchment-overlooked-inheritances-homebrew?p=1491092#post1491092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Final contribution, If I were going to try my hand at this idea, I'd probably land on something like &quot;The Haunting&quot;, where in a Beast collapses everything into a singular Chamber's physical location, &quot;The Nightmare&quot;, where in a Beast more tightly winds their Astral Chambers together and severs the Burrows to reality as much as possible, creating a shared nightmare people sleep their way into**, and &quot;The Labyrinth&quot;, which takes the way chambers work on both sides up to 11 sans their minotaur, whatever that means.<br /> <br /> EDIT: As a note on my own conceptions, I can see arguments for why a Beast would claim &quot;The Haunting&quot; and &quot;The Nightmare&quot;, but what I understand of my own &quot;Labyrinth&quot; concept? <a href=\"https://comicaurora.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/CH17_032_mercy.png\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;I didn't design them to do that. Who would, really?&quot;</a><br /> <br /> *Life Inheritances don't do this, of course, but they're openly intended to contrast the Legend Inheritances, so some of the rules are changed.<br /> **This is where &quot;place of power&quot; is arguable, because the Astral is a place-not-place.</div> </div> </div> </div>First off, upvote for the use of Aurora =D<br /> <br /> The Haunting and Nightmare is very close to what was originally the idea for the Entranchment and the Vacancy (very similar to The Retreat and The Merger).<br /> With the Vacancy, I didn't manage to figure out how to disconnect the Lair from the physical world entirely, due to thinking it still needed to gain Satiety somehow as a form of upkeep, or else fall into disrepair and fade away. I like your concept of the Nightmare much better.<br /> The idea of the Labyrinth as something entirely new and strange, perhaps even to the Dark Mother, and/or an entirely unintended result, is intriguing.<br /> (The following are probably more plot hooks than anything) Kind of the Lair becoming a new being itself, maybe a collection of Chambers that have a will when there are enough of them, who can connect to the Physical, but also 'hunt' and invade in the Astral? Expanding and engulfing other places, kind of like how deserts tend to grow. The more chambers it has, the more powerful and intelligent/sapient it becomes. Disconnecting Chambers makes them wither and 'die', with some repercussions for the corresponding physical location. <br /> Or like a virus, entering chambers and changing them to become like it and spread. However, growing inert/dying after a short while due to being unable to replenish Satiety at the rate they burn through it.<br /> <br /> Btw, I stumbled over your use of &quot;the mire&quot; earlier, absolutely adore that term, and think it must be used somehow somewhere. Rather than Labyrinth, your quest for becoming Incarnate end up in the Mire (not an Inheritance, maybe a persistent condition?)- an undesirable end, being a physical mixture of the Astral and Physical, imperfectly combined, lessened.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1490127-the-arrival-vacancy-and-entrenchment-overlooked-inheritances-homebrew?p=1491090#post1491090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Arrival (which probably also needs a different name really, the character hasn't gone somewhere new or anything) should exceedingly crippling to the Beast when they leave their Lair. To keep up with Arc's pithier comment, the Arrival seems like it should have a downside outside the Lair equal to if not greater than those bonuses in the Lair tantamount to being near suicidal for them to venture back to where their enemies can fight them without the protection of their boosted Lair.<br /> <br /> A relatively simple way you could make it momentous to even consider leaving their home: They take on both the Ravenous and Gorged Conditions as long as they're not home. They've invested so much of themselves into their Lair leaving robs them of all access to their powers, while also forcing them to feed, a lot, if they stay away for any amount of time.<br /> <br /> This also helps drive in the nail that this represents a final state of being. They have become their Lair, and if kept from it they will wither and die, while being apart from their dream-soul robs them of every ounce of supernatural might they had before.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the name will have to go. Essentially, you propose making this the shut-in option <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7593_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7593\" data-vbnamecard=\"7593\">Teatime</a> talked about? I mean, it makes sense. So, how about the Tether?<br /> Forgetting the use of conditions is one of my larger failures when tinkering (bumbling, rather) with mechanics. I like the idea of losing access to powers, and needing to Feed more when leaving the Lair. So just make a new condition based on those two? No powers at all outside chambers as per <i>Slumbering</i>, but also loses Kinship abilities (essentially, loses the Beast template save for Satiety instead of Integrity). In addition, as per <i>Ravenous</i>, they take 1L per day where they don't Feed and cannot heal Lethal/Agg at all, nor restore Willpower normally. Finally, gain the &quot;Obsession&quot; Condition, with a focus of returning to their Lair. That would serve as a harsh deterrent against leaving the Lair, while still making it somewhat possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-28T08:25:18-07:00","id":1491599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1490127-the-arrival-vacancy-and-entrenchment-overlooked-inheritances-homebrew?p=1491566#post1491566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(The following are probably more plot hooks than anything) Kind of the Lair becoming a new being itself, maybe a collection of Chambers that have a will when there are enough of them, who can connect to the Physical, but also 'hunt' and invade in the Astral? Expanding and engulfing other places, kind of like how deserts tend to grow. The more chambers it has, the more powerful and intelligent/sapient it becomes. Disconnecting Chambers makes them wither and 'die', with some repercussions for the corresponding physical location.<br /> Or like a virus, entering chambers and changing them to become like it and spread. However, growing inert/dying after a short while due to being unable to replenish Satiety at the rate they burn through it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm struck by the notion of an Inheritance that's sort of a mix of a sentient Apex Trait and Hunting Grounds/Badlands from <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/395104/Wild-Hunt-Gangrel?affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Wild Hunt: Gangrel</a>, like a Primordial disaster spreading through a hive, freaking out the dreamscape, and spinning off Horrorspawn and Heralds to a Horror that isn't there anymore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-30T08:24:50-07:00","id":1491906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1490127-the-arrival-vacancy-and-entrenchment-overlooked-inheritances-homebrew?p=1491599#post1491599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm struck by the notion of an Inheritance that's sort of a mix of a sentient Apex Trait and Hunting Grounds/Badlands from <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/395104/Wild-Hunt-Gangrel?affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Wild Hunt: Gangrel</a>, like a Primordial disaster spreading through a hive, freaking out the dreamscape, and spinning off Horrorspawn and Heralds to a Horror that isn't there anymore.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, something like that. The hungry hunting grounds, spreading and hunting through anything that has resonances with the Chambers present at Inheritance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-31T13:41:30-07:00","id":1492028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1490127-the-arrival-vacancy-and-entrenchment-overlooked-inheritances-homebrew?p=1491599#post1491599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm struck by the notion of an Inheritance that's sort of a mix of a sentient Apex Trait and Hunting Grounds/Badlands from <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/395104/Wild-Hunt-Gangrel?affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Wild Hunt: Gangrel</a>, like a Primordial disaster spreading through a hive, freaking out the dreamscape, and spinning off Horrorspawn and Heralds to a Horror that isn't there anymore.</div> </div> </div> </div>This feels like just the right thing. The Heralds/Horrorspawn to a no-longer-existing Horror is such a nice touch that you can play off in so many different ways. I like!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-01T14:13:51-07:00","id":1492117,"title":"","content":"[DELETED POST]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/22.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":25791,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","user":"TerrorCooper","date":".  Accidentally double-posted with an improperly formed post. 09-01-2022, 05:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","name":"TerrorCooper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-01T14:33:34-07:00","id":1492119,"title":"","content":"Just finished reading this thread (somewhat), and I. Am. <b><i><u>LOVING</u></i></b> <b><i><u>IT!!!!</u></i></b><br /> <br /> Also, here's a neat idea I just thought of; what do y'all think would occur if someone were to somehow achieve both the Incarnate Inheritance, <i>and</i> the 'Labyrinth' Inheritance, at the same time? Do you think it would even be possible? I mean, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar99_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"99\" data-vbnamecard=\"99\">ArcaneArts</a> <i>did</i> write/say that the latter was the way of, and I quote;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1490127-the-arrival-vacancy-and-entrenchment-overlooked-inheritances-homebrew?p=1491092#post1491092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> [...] [taking] the way chambers work on both sides up to 11 sans their minotaur [...]</div> </div> </div> </div>Now, I don't know about you, but that last part makes me think that there might be <i>just</i> enough wiggle room, even if its barely by the skin of one's teeth, for a member of the Begotten to try incarnating themselves, alongside attempting to 'labyrinth-up' their Lair for even greater results.<br /> <br /> I mean, a maze can be dangerous enough in the right conditions/circumstances <i>without</i> there being any 'guardians' present, so what if you were to just... add the minotaur back into the equation?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/22.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","name":"TerrorCooper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-01T15:46:50-07:00","id":1492124,"title":"","content":"The RAW (which I'm disinclined to argue with or change if I had the power to do so) is that, though the Dark Mother's mansion has many rooms, you only get the one if you claim it, not multiple, and that asides, the psychospiritual metaphysics around Inheritance makes arguably the pinnacle of ego Inheritance very at odds with the pinnacle of death-of-ego Inheritance.<br /> <br /> In this model, we're concerned with the Lair as expressed through the Horror versus as expressed through the Chambers. That's not a small distinction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-03T03:40:14-07:00","id":1492208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1490127-the-arrival-vacancy-and-entrenchment-overlooked-inheritances-homebrew?p=1492124#post1492124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The RAW (which I'm disinclined to argue with or change if I had the power to do so) is that, though the Dark Mother's mansion has many rooms, you only get the one if you claim it, not multiple, and that asides, the psychospiritual metaphysics around Inheritance makes arguably the pinnacle of ego Inheritance very at odds with the pinnacle of death-of-ego Inheritance.<br /> <br /> In this model, we're concerned with the Lair as expressed through the Horror versus as expressed through the Chambers. That's not a small distinction.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, thanks for clarifying that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/22.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","name":"TerrorCooper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}